speechtext:
My right hon. friend will observe that the judgment of the territorial court sitting in banc was final and conclusive if that court was unanimous;
I but if the court was not unanimous, then

there was to be an appeal direct to the Supreme Court of Canada. As the court may be reduced to one judge under this statute, the appeal is given in all cases.

